    "long_instructions": "Now, encode the location data.\r\n\r\n**☑️ Do This:**\r\n- Use `OneHotEncoder` to create a one-hot encoder.\r\n- Use your one-hot encoder to encode the `location` data.\r\n- Add your encoding to the `features` list.\r\n- Run the program to check your work. You should see your encoding appear in the printed feature matrix.\r\n\r\n**💻 Coding Tip**\r\n\r\nRemember that `OneHotEncoder` is a class from `scikit-learn`. You can use it to create and configure an object to encode your data using a one-hot encoding:\r\n\r\n```\r\nencoder = OneHotEncoder()\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlso remember you’ll need to create a matrix to encode:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlocation_matrix = []\r\nfor row in data:\r\n  location_matrix.append([row[\"location\"]])\r\n```\r\n\r\nThen, using the `fit_transform` function gives you your encoded data:\r\n\r\n```\r\ntype_encoding = type_encoder.fit_transform(location_matrix)\r\n```",
    "bubble_choice_description": "Help a food truck predict how many sales they’ll make on a given day.",
